<title>USA: Tracor Q1 oper shr diluted up.</title>
<headline>Tracor Q1 oper shr diluted up.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tracor, Inc.</p>
<p>				Three months ended MArch 31</p>
<p>			     1997	     1996</p>
<p>Net sales		$297,464,000	$229,047,000</p>
<p>Earnings before</p>
<p>interest and</p>
<p>    income taxes	 26,115,000	  19,447,000</p>
<p>Income before</p>
<p>extraordinary item     10,264,000	   7,661,000</p>
<p>Extraordinary loss</p>
<p>from early</p>
<p>extinguishment of</p>
<p>debt, net of income</p>
<p> tax benefit of $7,084  9,985,000		   ---</p>
<p>    Net income	 $    279,000    $    7,661,000</p>
<p>Income before</p>
<p>    extraordinary item	  $.38		  $.32</p>
<p>	Extraordinary loss	(.37)		  ---</p>
<p>	Net income		  $.01		  $.32</p>
<p>Weighted average common and common equivalent</p>
<p>shares used in</p>
<p>    EPS calculation	26,767,000	  24,878,000</p>
<p>NOTE: During the quarter, Tracor restructured its debt by completing the private placement of $250 million of 8-1/2 percent Senior Subordinated Notes due 2007 and using the proceeds to pay off the company's 10-7/8 percent Senior Subordinated Notes due 2001 and bank debt. The accounting for the debt restructuring requires the company to write off all the remaining unamortized costs associated with the old bonds and bank loans, resulting in a one-time charge of $0.37 per share.</p>
</text>
